1. Abstract

The Proton–Laser Interaction & Cosmic Data Integration Engine (v1.2) is a hybrid astrophysical–plasma simulation architecture integrating cosmic dataset ingestion, proton–laser acceleration physics, particle‑in‑cell (PIC) solvers, magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) coupling, GPU‑accelerated computation, and zero‑trust encryption. The system models proton acceleration mechanisms (TNSA, RPA), laser–plasma interaction zones, cosmic‑environment boundary conditions, and encrypted high‑performance computing workflows. This white sheet presents the architecture, physics foundations, computational methodology, and stability governance underlying the engine.

